  "worked_solution": "Notice that the dividend is missing the $x$-term. So, we write it using a zero coefficient, as follows:\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+0x+16\n$$\n\nUsing the method of polynomial division, we obtain the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,x-4 \\\\  & x+4\\,\\enclose{longdiv}{\\,\\,{x}^{2}+0x+16} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{{x}^{2}+4x}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,-\\,4x+16 \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,{-\\,4x-16}_{\u2015} \\\\  & \\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,\\,32\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the missing expressions are\n\n$\\,$ $x-4\\,$ and $\\,-4x+16.$",
